{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1029878-call-lightning-and-the-case-of-pointless-potency","id":1029878,"title":"Call Lightning and the Case of Pointless Potency","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-10T19:51:11-08:00","id":1029878,"title":"Call Lightning and the Case of Pointless Potency","content":"So I've come across this a few times, most recently in Call Lightning (Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022). We have a spell that uses Potency as its primary factor, but Potency doesn't seem to affect the actual spell. As far as I can tell, we have a spell that needs to have an existing storm to draw from; it can't really be dodged (though the writing is kind of ambiguous on that point); and it does a blanket 10 bashing damage (ouch).<br /> <br /> But Potency seems to be absent. And I know that I've come across this a couple of times. I assume that there are just spells that have no real primary factor and rather than say &quot;primary factor: none,&quot; we plug in Duration or Potency to fill the spot. But you know what happens when you assume. <br /> <br /> So am I wrong? Do you guys use Potency in this spell? Have I misunderstood a simple mechanic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1752-mofous","name":"mofous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1752_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T20:12:41-08:00","id":1029890,"title":"","content":"Spells with immediate effects aren't really set up to immediately build into the &quot;spell recurs once per casting interval&quot; trick and therefore use Potency.<br /> <br /> Two notable sideways applications: Call Lightning is pretty much always a viable spell to cast sympathetically, and can apply the caster's Nimbus Tilt to any non-sympathetic target who's not rocking above-average Resolve if they happen to be using Mage Sight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 01-10-2017, 11:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T20:13:23-08:00","id":1029891,"title":"","content":"Potency does seem to filled in for &quot;none&quot; in that sense. There are some mechanical implications of it, but I wouldn't expect it to come up much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T17:22:03-08:00","id":1030338,"title":"","content":"Okay, at the very least I can assume I'm not crazy. I'll try not to worry too much about it and trust my instincts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1752-mofous","name":"mofous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1752_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T03:51:44-08:00","id":1030510,"title":"","content":"Remember that Creative Thaumaturgy mentions that Storyteller may gate certain powerful, narrative effects behind Potency. It's perfectly viable for a GM to say that in order to call lightning from that storm of century, you need Potency X.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T10:04:27-08:00","id":1030639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1029878-call-lightning-and-the-case-of-pointless-potency?p=1030510#post1030510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that Creative Thaumaturgy mentions that Storyteller may gate certain powerful, narrative effects behind Potency. It's perfectly viable for a GM to say that in order to call lightning from that storm of century, you need Potency X.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes a lot of sense. I think I glossed over that, but It's definitely something to consider. I also recently let someone try to dodge the lightning strike at a penalty equal to the spell's Potency. Basically letting the Potency determine how quickly the spell took effect and how hard it was to dive out of the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1752-mofous","name":"mofous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1752_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T19:57:39-08:00","id":1031941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mofous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1029878-call-lightning-and-the-case-of-pointless-potency?p=1030639#post1030639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This makes a lot of sense. I think I glossed over that, but It's definitely something to consider. I also recently let someone try to dodge the lightning strike at a penalty equal to the spell's Potency. Basically letting the Potency determine how quickly the spell took effect and how hard it was to dive out of the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lightning travels at ~3,700 miles per second, even spells and abilities that let you dodge bullets (~2,500 feet per second, about 0.01% the speed of lightning) would be useless against a lightning strike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T22:31:31-08:00","id":1031995,"title":"","content":"While in general I agree with the point that you can't &quot;dodge&quot; lightning, the spell in specific says that it provides warning and that you can avoid the attack if lightning couldn't logically hit you. This implies characters targeted with it have some chance to get to cover if there is anything appropriate available. Calling for a roll to do so and penalizing it by Potency to make Potency matter for the spell isn't out of line with the spell as written and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T13:22:45-08:00","id":1032873,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1029878-call-lightning-and-the-case-of-pointless-potency?p=1031941#post1031941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lightning travels at ~3,700 miles per second, even spells and abilities that let you dodge bullets (~2,500 feet per second, about 0.01% the speed of lightning) would be useless against a lightning strike.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was the line <b>&quot;While the lightning bolt itself is all but unavoidable, the crackling build-up of energy gives a target warning&quot;</b> that inspired the ruling. It also would have meant certain death for the PC, which would have been rather anticlimactic at the moment. </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1752-mofous","name":"mofous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1752_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T00:50:32-08:00","id":1036482,"title":"","content":"You could also make the size of the area struck by the lightning scale with Potency, inflicting less but still dangerous amount of damage. Or make the lightning be able to penetrate ceilings that its victim is hiding under, also relative to Potency.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, those are probably more apt as Reach effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T01:03:45-08:00","id":1036487,"title":"","content":"Area of effect is a spell factor. Letting lighting pass through things that lightning can't pass through really doesn't seem like a Reach effect for this particular spell (which is essentially about compelling a natural lightning strike to happen). There's still things like combinations and conjunctional effects for certain things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}